      "assistant_text": "According to [[write-journal]], the Guarded Write Journal describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. \n\nSpecifically, it works like this:\n\n- Before any file is overwritten, the guarded tool executor records the file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either the file\u0027s previous content, or a note that it didn\u0027t exist.\n- If the agent run later fails (due to exceeding turn limits, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal rolls every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content where it existed, and deleting newly created files.\n- This provides **all-or-nothing semantics** for writes without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as the transaction log during a single run, held only in process memory.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write capability, but the journal type is part of the shared agent runtime library.",
